{"type":"Film","id":"FR2023_223","slug":"fr2023-223-ma-france-a-moi","title":{"native":"Ma France à moi","english":"My Motherland"},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2023-12-20","year":2023},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Benoît Cohen","slug":"benoit-cohen","name":"Benoît Cohen","birthYear":1969,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]}],"genre":["Drama"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/157/28/269469/format_page/ma-france-a-moi.jpg","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0XGnEAMiwqU"},"synopsis":{"native":"France, la soixantaine, vit seule dans son appartement bourgeois de l’est parisien. Lorsqu’elle entend parler à la radio d’une association qui met en contact des personnes réfugiées sans logement et celles ayant la possibilité de les accueillir, elle décroche son téléphone pour se porter volontaire. Quelques jours plus tard, Reza, jeune afghan d’à peine vingt ans, débarque dans sa vie. Ces deux êtres, qui n’ont rien en commun, vont devoir apprendre à vivre ensemble…","english":"France has been living alone in her apartment since her husband’s death. When she hears on the radio that an NGO is putting in touch homeless migrants and people who are willing to welcome them, she decides, against her family’s opinion to welcome Reza, a young Afghan broken by war and exile. Two worlds meet, and they begin to hold each other’s hands."},"production":[{"country":"France","share":"Majority coproducer"}],"characters":[{"id":"FR2023_223_01","film":"FR2023_223","person":{"id":"Fanny Ardant","slug":"fanny-ardant","name":"Fanny Ardant","birthYear":1949,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Female identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[{"film":{"slug":"fr2022-021-les-jeunes-amants","title":{"native":"Les Jeunes Amants"}},"year":2023,"award":"César du cinéma","category":"Unknown","result":"Nominated"},{"film":{"slug":"fr2020-091-adn","title":{"native":"ADN"}},"year":2021,"award":"César du ciném